  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "How to read this view",
      "items": [
        "Each row is an independent guarded transition, not a chronological sequence across rows. Repeated phase labels name the same underlying phase; aliases prevent unrelated rules from sharing ambiguous drawing corridors. The normal-procedure view supplies the connected happy path."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Reading this view",
      "items": [
        "snake_case labels are real session.phase strings. Nodes in the 'conceptual step' legend group, or with tag 'conceptual'/'phase group', are not phase strings.",
        "Pilot calls move a phase only after telemetry confirms the claim (_at_hold, _at_crossing, _lined_up). Take-off, landing and vacating come from the mission track alone (airfield.py 44-50)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Rules",
      "items": [
        "Not in the air during an airborne arrival phase, never seen airborne, with priority and on the ground here: 'emergency on the ground', phase landed. Without priority the session closes as 'not airborne' (846-856).",
        "Seen airborne and on the ground here: touchdown, then landed. On the ground at another airfield: 'landing not observed', session closed (857-863).",
        "A land event naming another place closes the session (811-816).",
        "A cancel while occupying a runway sets phase cancelled with vacating. The session closes once vacating is observed or reported (1540-1543, 1800-1805).",
        "A departure request from an arrival needs vacated, taxi_in_clearance or taxi_in, on the ground here. Otherwise it is refused (1596-1599)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Transition evidence (file lines)",
      "items": [
        "grounded \u2192 landed: priority + parked here (849-853); grounded sample here (857-860)",
        "grounded \u2192 closed: parked at enrolment (854-855); 861-862",
        "land elsewhere: 814-816, 861-862",
        "cancel: vacating = True (1540-1543); observed or reported (1800-1805)",
        "handover: ground here (1596-1599)"
      ]
    }
  ]
